infographic hierarchy-mindmap-level-gradient-compact-card
data
  title ATAM-lite: three words for competing -ilities
  desc Name what each architectural decision is before you ship it — the vocabulary that turns "good" or "risky" into something precise
  root
    label An architectural decision
    children
      - label Sensitivity point — one attribute
        desc Strongly moves a single quality attribute; the rest barely change. E.g. partitioning the event log by customer ID tunes per-customer query latency alone.
      - label Tradeoff point — opposing attributes
        desc Improves some attributes while degrading others. E.g. event sourcing buys auditability and temporal queries at the cost of modifiability and operational simplicity.
      - label Risk — a plausible future failure
        desc Lets an attribute miss its required level in a plausible-but-unrealized scenario. E.g. an immutable PII log once right-to-erasure becomes law.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f43f5e
